From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tsuji Riya <tsuji.riya@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] nvmem: layouts: u-boot-env: parse wifiaddr as a MAC
 address too

Some boot loaders keep the Wi-Fi MAC address in a "wifiaddr" variable
next to "ethaddr" (the D-Link DSM-232 vendor U-Boot does). Give it the
same post-processing as ethaddr, so that a Wi-Fi node can take it as its
mac-address nvmem cell.
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/nvmem/layouts/u-boot,env.yaml  | 10 ++++++++++
 drivers/nvmem/layouts/u-boot-env.c                     |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/nvmem/layouts/u-boot,env.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/nvmem/layouts/u-boot,env.yaml
index e9e75c38b..a598a7640 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/nvmem/layouts/u-boot,env.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/nvmem/layouts/u-boot,env.yaml
@@ -62,6 +62,16 @@ properties:
         description: The first argument is a MAC address offset.
         const: 1
 
+  wifiaddr:
+    type: object
+    description: Wi-Fi interface MAC address.
+    additionalProperties: false
+
+    properties:
+      "#nvmem-cell-cells":
+        description: The first argument is a MAC address offset.
+        const: 1
+
 allOf:
   - if:
       properties:
diff --git a/drivers/nvmem/layouts/u-boot-env.c b/drivers/nvmem/layouts/u-boot-env.c
index f27f387bb..a3e649cac 100644
--- a/drivers/nvmem/layouts/u-boot-env.c
+++ b/drivers/nvmem/layouts/u-boot-env.c
@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@ static int u_boot_env_parse_cells(struct device *dev, struct nvmem_device *nvmem
 		info.offset = data_offset + value - data;
 		info.bytes = strlen(value);
 		info.np = of_get_child_by_name(dev->of_node, info.name);
-		if (!strcmp(var, "ethaddr")) {
+		if (!strcmp(var, "ethaddr") || !strcmp(var, "wifiaddr")) {
 			info.raw_len = strlen(value);
 			info.bytes = ETH_ALEN;
 			info.read_post_process = u_boot_env_read_post_process_ethaddr;
